WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.558 --> 00:00:03.227
- He started his business with $20,000

00:00:03.227 --> 00:00:06.023
that his wife and his
friend helped him raise.

00:00:06.023 --> 00:00:08.516
He's the first mainline China entrepreneur

00:00:08.516 --> 00:00:11.353
to be featured on the
cover of Forbes magazine.

00:00:11.353 --> 00:00:12.826
He's the richest man in China,

00:00:12.826 --> 00:00:15.002
and the 18th richest man in the world,

00:00:15.002 --> 00:00:19.401
with an estimated fortune
of $29.7 billion dollars.

00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:22.271
He's Jack Ma, founder of Alibaba.com,

00:00:22.271 --> 00:00:25.155
and here are his 10 rules for success.

00:00:25.155 --> 00:00:26.818
(loud explosion)

00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:29.604
(rooster crowing)

00:00:29.604 --> 00:00:32.687
- When I graduated from universities,

00:00:33.698 --> 00:00:37.342
and for three years I tried,
failed in the universities.

00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:41.092
So I applied jobs for
30 times, got rejected.

00:00:42.597 --> 00:00:45.409
I went for police, they
say, "No, you're not good."

00:00:45.409 --> 00:00:49.232
I went, even the KFC,
when KFC came to China,

00:00:49.232 --> 00:00:50.582
come to our city.

00:00:50.582 --> 00:00:51.820
- [Interviewer] You applied.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.987
- 24 people went for the
job, 23 people were accepted.

00:00:57.652 --> 00:00:59.455
I was the only guy.

00:00:59.455 --> 00:01:00.288
(audience laughing)

00:01:00.288 --> 00:01:03.600
And we went for police, 5
people, 4 of them accepted.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.193
I was the only guy they're not receiving.

00:01:06.193 --> 00:01:09.292
So to me, being turned down, rejected.

00:01:09.292 --> 00:01:12.829
Oh, by the way, I told you
that I applied for Harvard

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:14.761
for 10 times, rejected.

00:01:14.761 --> 00:01:15.594
(audience laughing)

00:01:15.594 --> 00:01:17.715
I know I would be rejected,
I just wanted to say that.

00:01:17.715 --> 00:01:19.456
- [Interviewer] They're sorry now.

00:01:19.456 --> 00:01:20.318
(laughing)

00:01:20.318 --> 00:01:21.964
10 times you wrote them and said,

00:01:21.964 --> 00:01:23.408
"I'd like to come to Harvard."

00:01:23.408 --> 00:01:24.241
- Yeah.

00:01:24.241 --> 00:01:25.481
And then I told myself, someday

00:01:25.481 --> 00:01:27.691
I should go teach there, maybe.

00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:28.674
(audience laughing)

00:01:28.674 --> 00:01:31.507
We have a secret code for success.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:37.199
Just like open sesame is
the secret code for Alibaba,

00:01:37.199 --> 00:01:41.657
the secret code for everybody
is keep your dream alive

00:01:41.657 --> 00:01:44.923
because it might come through some day.

00:01:44.923 --> 00:01:46.627
This is what the secret code is.

00:01:46.627 --> 00:01:49.303
- [Interviewer] What do you
think you core competence is?

00:01:49.303 --> 00:01:50.553
- It's culture.

00:01:52.037 --> 00:01:54.344
It's not the technology, I
think technology is a tool.

00:01:54.344 --> 00:01:56.451
The core competence of our company

00:01:56.451 --> 00:02:00.618
is we have grown from 18 people
to now, 20,000 young people.

00:02:02.273 --> 00:02:06.046
And we focus a lot on
the value, the mission

00:02:06.046 --> 00:02:08.076
and making sure the
culture, everybody work

00:02:08.076 --> 00:02:12.082
for helping others, instead
of just making money.

00:02:12.082 --> 00:02:14.014
People don't like it.

00:02:14.014 --> 00:02:16.497
So many people I talk to
at that time for Alipay,

00:02:16.497 --> 00:02:20.247
this is the stupidest
idea you have ever got,

00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:23.933
but I say, "Whether stupid or clever,

00:02:23.933 --> 00:02:26.183
"as long as people use it."

00:02:27.072 --> 00:02:31.155
Now we have 800 million
people using this Alipay.

00:02:32.039 --> 00:02:34.617
I learn a lot of things from movies.

00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:37.645
I learned how to make a speech

00:02:37.645 --> 00:02:42.171
from the movie called
Bodyguard, Whitney Houston.

00:02:42.171 --> 00:02:45.135
When she sings the songs,
I look at her, wow.

00:02:45.135 --> 00:02:47.615
That's the way that you make a speech.

00:02:47.615 --> 00:02:50.446
'Cause I never know how to make speech.

00:02:50.446 --> 00:02:52.393
'Cause I'm not actor.

00:02:52.393 --> 00:02:55.933
But when I saw the movie, I say wow.

00:02:55.933 --> 00:02:59.223
If you sing from your heart,
if you sing naturally,

00:02:59.223 --> 00:03:02.056
if you are yourself, so I realize.

00:03:03.865 --> 00:03:05.908
And I learn a lot from the movies.

00:03:05.908 --> 00:03:07.923
I even learn from The Godfathers.

00:03:07.923 --> 00:03:11.040
My favorite movie is Forrest Gump.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.060
These are the things I learned so much.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.245
Then I would discuss about the muse,

00:03:17.245 --> 00:03:19.713
the inspirations we got from movies.

00:03:19.713 --> 00:03:22.760
- What kinds of business
ideas have you said no to?

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.061
- I'm saying no to a lot
of ideas because as a CEO,

00:03:26.061 --> 00:03:28.226
I have to say no to opportunities,

00:03:28.226 --> 00:03:29.681
because if I say yes,

00:03:29.681 --> 00:03:32.434
I probably get 5,000
opportunities everyday.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:36.595
But whether yes or no,
everything based on the mission,

00:03:36.595 --> 00:03:39.418
helping doing business easier.

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.412
If it's on that, we'll consider.

00:03:41.412 --> 00:03:42.888
If somebody come and say,

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:45.158
"Can you, we'll make a lot of money."

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.090
I'm not interested.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.779
- [Interviewer] Why did
you call it Alibaba?

00:03:48.779 --> 00:03:49.612
- Alibaba?

00:03:50.792 --> 00:03:54.806
Well, when I started, I
think, Internet is global,

00:03:54.806 --> 00:03:59.796
we should have a global name,
and a name that interesting.

00:03:59.796 --> 00:04:02.321
At that time, the best name was Yahoo.

00:04:02.321 --> 00:04:03.450
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.494
- So I've been thinking for many days,

00:04:05.494 --> 00:04:07.290
suddenly think Alibaba is a good name.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.990
I happened to be in
San Francisco that day,

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.972
Having lunch, and a waitress come.

00:04:13.972 --> 00:04:16.218
I ask her, "Do you know about Alibaba?"

00:04:16.218 --> 00:04:17.196
She say, "Yes."

00:04:17.196 --> 00:04:18.527
I say, "What is Alibaba?"

00:04:18.527 --> 00:04:20.695
She say, "Open sesame."

00:04:20.695 --> 00:04:21.678
Good!

00:04:21.678 --> 00:04:24.485
So I went on the street,
ask about 10, 20 people.

00:04:24.485 --> 00:04:28.652
They all know about Alibaba,
40 thieves and open sesame,

00:04:29.997 --> 00:04:33.731
and I think this a good
name, and start with A,

00:04:33.731 --> 00:04:36.329
whatever you talk about,
Alibaba's always top.

00:04:36.329 --> 00:04:37.339
(audience laughing)

00:04:37.339 --> 00:04:40.708
We believe the core company
different from the Wall Street.

00:04:40.708 --> 00:04:42.581
We believe customer, number one,

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.452
employee, number two,
shareholder, number three.

00:04:44.452 --> 00:04:45.707
- Customer one, employee two,

00:04:45.707 --> 00:04:47.335
shareholder three.
- Shareholder, number three.

00:04:47.335 --> 00:04:49.084
Yeah, again, this is my religion.

00:04:49.084 --> 00:04:52.429
It's the customer that pay us the money,

00:04:52.429 --> 00:04:55.108
it's the employees that
drive the innovation,

00:04:55.108 --> 00:04:57.147
it's the shareholder always say.

00:04:57.147 --> 00:05:00.795
I remember the day before the IPO,

00:05:00.795 --> 00:05:03.253
and a lot of people say,
"Jack, give us the shares,

00:05:03.253 --> 00:05:04.984
"we were long term shareholders."

00:05:04.984 --> 00:05:08.285
But when the crisis came,
these guys run as soon as--

00:05:08.285 --> 00:05:09.661
- [Interviewer] They ran away.

00:05:09.661 --> 00:05:12.987
- My people stayed, customers stayed.

00:05:12.987 --> 00:05:16.035
- Next I want to tell young people.

00:05:16.035 --> 00:05:20.406
Most people complain,
"Where's the opportunity?"

00:05:20.406 --> 00:05:22.615
People started complaining,
some people complain,

00:05:22.615 --> 00:05:26.493
some people start to change
themselves, changing others.

00:05:26.493 --> 00:05:30.016
Where the opportunity is is
where the complaints are.

00:05:30.016 --> 00:05:32.428
Where the trouble,
where's the opportunity.

00:05:32.428 --> 00:05:34.678
And I always believed that.

00:07:48.089 --> 00:07:49.338
- Thank you guys for watching.

00:07:49.338 --> 00:07:51.137
The question of the day for you is

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:53.262
I want to know what kind of rejection

00:07:53.262 --> 00:07:56.069
you've had to overcome in your
life and in your business.

00:07:56.069 --> 00:07:57.915
If you've had to overcome
a lot of rejection

00:07:57.915 --> 00:07:59.288
and you have a special story to share,

00:07:59.288 --> 00:08:00.344
I'd love to hear from you

00:08:00.344 --> 00:08:02.007
if you want to leave a comment below.

00:08:02.007 --> 00:08:03.662
I made this video on Jack Ma

00:08:03.662 --> 00:08:05.923
because Jeff Lee-Yang asked me to.

00:08:05.923 --> 00:08:07.911
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:08:07.911 --> 00:08:09.885
that you want me to
profile, leave a comment,

00:08:09.885 --> 00:08:12.204
let me know what you think
and I'll see what I can do.

00:08:12.204 --> 00:08:13.785
And of course, if you like this video

00:08:13.785 --> 00:08:15.626
and you want to see more,
don't forget to subscribe

00:08:15.626 --> 00:08:17.228
to the newsletter and the channel.

00:08:17.228 --> 00:08:19.466
Thank you for watching,
continue to believe,

00:08:19.466 --> 00:08:21.817
have an amazing day,
and I hope you'll start

00:08:21.817 --> 00:08:23.489
your day again with me tomorrow

00:08:23.489 --> 00:08:25.386
with another inspirational video.

00:08:25.386 --> 00:08:27.677
(loud explosion)

